{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model forecasts are systematically below realized prices across most of the 30-day horizon, especially during uptrends/rallies. Apply an upward level shift (positive bias correction), larger in the first ~20 days.",
    "Trend underreaction / lag: when history transitions into a rising regime, the model increases too slowly and misses the magnitude of the move. Add a momentum/trend-following adjustment (e.g., proportional to recent 5–10d slope) to reduce lag.",
    "Rally peak underestimation: around local highs the model remains several EUR/tCO2 too low (misses the peak amplitude). Use a convex adjustment in strong positive momentum regimes (bigger uplift when recent returns are strongly positive).",
    "Late-horizon overshoot: in some cases the model drifts too high at the far end (≈days 25–30) while realized prices mean-revert/lower. Damp long-horizon forecasts toward a mean/anchor (e.g., blend with recent average) to avoid end-of-horizon inflation.",
    "Asymmetric error: model handles down-moves better than up-moves; corrections should be regime-dependent (stronger upward correction in bullish regimes, minimal change in bearish/flat regimes)."
  ]
}
